where $V(s)$ is the Laplace transform of $v(t)$.
Then
\[V(s) \left( 1 - \frac{1}{sC} - \frac{1}{sL} - \frac{1}{sR} \right) = \frac{V_i(s)}{s}\]
\[V(s) = \frac{V_i(s)}{s \left( 1 - \frac{1}{sC} - \frac{1}{sL} - \frac{1}{sR} \right)} = \frac{V_i(s)}{s} \cdot \frac{1}{1 - \frac{1}{C} - \frac{1}{L} - \frac{1}{R}} = \frac{V_i(s)}{s \left( \frac{1}{C} + \frac{1}{L} + \frac{1}{R} \right)}\]
